# Typing-Race environment
#
# F1 (001-typing-core) needs NOTHING here. It has no server, no account, no network call at
# runtime: progress lives in the browser behind the ProgressStore seam. That is deliberate, and it
# is what makes the requirements' "starts from a single documented command" true — `pnpm install`
# then `pnpm dev`, with no setup step in between.
#
# The variables below arrive with F2 (002-accounts-and-progress) and are listed now so the shape is
# known. Copy this file to .env.local and fill them in only once F2 lands. Never commit .env.local;
# only this example file is tracked. Both values are public by design — the anon key is protected by
# row-level security, not by secrecy — but they still stay out of git.

# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
